      "id": 1,
      "text": "Iron Station earned its name from the iron mines that once powered a bustling train depot in the 1800s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron_Station%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The historic Iron Station Depot, built in 1862, still stands as a reminder of the town’s mining heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://nearbylens.com/cities/usa/nc/iron_station/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Iron Station sits on a ridge in the Piedmont region, draining northeast to Dellinger Branch and southwest to Hoyle Creek.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iron_Station%2C_North_Carolina"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Iron Station’s small population of about 1,000 residents keeps the town’s close‑knit, heritage‑celebrating culture alive.",
